[{"id":"VRCE-5-38-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing the speech of the high-souled offspring of the Wind-god, Sītā resembling a daughter of the celestials, said in words fraught with her welfare.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c12467a275b0d9c61d8e04152ae24af198171d264c7aea2dd9dee4ad6f558b6e","compact":"65df68d15af54090ed0b9b4e76762361dd1c1d2fa8bd1d70c26f470fb58597e7","nasal":"65df68d15af54090ed0b9b4e76762361dd1c1d2fa8bd1d70c26f470fb58597e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":2,"english":"Even as the Earth with corn half-way towards harvest is gladdened on receipt of showers, have I, O monkey, been gladdened on seeing you that speakest sweetly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"37817ec7f1c038cdcccb0fd0a3f39d14ee91e3829d4c0798b6428571deaaddf6","compact":"79063bbb1aedd57abbd541a1998a812984af5cd05edda9313615ec6bcb0bdd72","nasal":"79063bbb1aedd57abbd541a1998a812984af5cd05edda9313615ec6bcb0bdd72"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":3,"english":"Do you so dispense your kindness to me that, with my desire attained, I may touch that tigerlike one with my body reduced by grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"324072c9f915096faaf8f6bdc5a4eae7bc53d409af150d6c697545a88ecb48fc","compact":"03419b671541b00e8bbba4d71eed792170dc402a24d0aa2f45a22466852422a3","nasal":"03419b671541b00e8bbba4d71eed792170dc402a24d0aa2f45a22466852422a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":4,"english":"O foremost of monkeys, present this sign to Rāma, and tell him also for a sign that he had in ire hurled the dart which destroyed a single eye of the crow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"48907af33f8f1ae8d730ac09b19d05c61d215e7dd71e51038d89ca20bdadbc3f","compact":"546a601745804da68336512af653ae27a708e80eb05b7c4a8426b30f577dd118","nasal":"546a601745804da68336512af653ae27a708e80eb05b7c4a8426b30f577dd118"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":5,"english":"And tell him also, (Sītă wishes Hanuman to use her own language to Rama) 'On my (first) tilaka having been wiped out, you didst paint beside my cheek another cheek another made of red arsenic—this you You remember.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e17aa2b841b85fb633d4873222a7b87af9920d83fb567d5cc702d66b58767d19","compact":"2ea0dfb399f0d55681cb6f3d894f81097c81118ed2efdead154c89d9024cf026","nasal":"61b82b219289ccac2e2da814e90022ee66dbd5ebc90b091b53dc5fc0949b9fcc"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":6,"english":"Why, O you endowed with prowess, resembling Indra the Great or Varuņa, do you disregard the ravished Sītā, sitting in the midst of Raksasa?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fcae0ae8a94eb8ad039b93085262613985f9880784112737677da5e07327759d","compact":"9621040c9eab992828bbd26b7bbf2004cd1cecd794f2e12ee6d333954c5804c4","nasal":"66373a6c5ca25b1c97d9093cb88e3c8e08fafd7ed7791ac5e1de4ffcc9a6f3b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":7,"english":"This jewel for the head I had preserved with care. In my misfortune, O sinless one, I used to inspire cheerfulness by a sight a sight of this, resembling yourself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fe99dd02a0877fba441276b673e8cfa4b533532bdfd3be863b5d52d23039cda9","compact":"e0eb29f9227a85a53a926174ee7bd9a3692f8cfa8932c0eef808191f44caf7e4","nasal":"e0eb29f9227a85a53a926174ee7bd9a3692f8cfa8932c0eef808191f44caf7e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":8,"english":"This graceful water-sprung (gem) I part from. Hereafter, overwhelmed with grief, I shall not be able to live.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"01d2e1880e7663e7b085a2716979f790b010303920d5ef780b341663b9bb0de7","compact":"89862c5bd38dfd1a1ddbfd96d9ddc891f85bbf09051f3ee0e20ceca1b341bd3f","nasal":"89862c5bd38dfd1a1ddbfd96d9ddc891f85bbf09051f3ee0e20ceca1b341bd3f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":9,"english":"For you only do I bear insufferable miseries, heart-cleaving speech, and companionship with Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.708,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84d678acdb19b0efabf2779385114c64c6ca1518a01385214e243691096b919a","compact":"2b3dba5395e79df3873df95c1c8aed66192d47b508fce2c44851e2a996629a1a","nasal":"2b3dba5395e79df3873df95c1c8aed66192d47b508fce2c44851e2a996629a1a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":10,"english":"O destroyer of enemies, for a month longer will I maintain being. Beyond that, О king's son, bereft of you, I will not live.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d60172118685b29e996399b71bc1cceff1693c89e951791d40dc1b1e39dd1440","compact":"b5bf3080f541b8e0b0bdf229eda9f3a14cf80fbfb248ab8d1064591c19125b55","nasal":"b5bf3080f541b8e0b0bdf229eda9f3a14cf80fbfb248ab8d1064591c19125b55"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":11,"english":"This Raksasa king is dreadful. (This being so), if I hear you tarrying, I would not live for a moment.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.708,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1bad382d8190d7a5840957c2392e9a275b8791c7ef9509efa0a43e3d6b143c6e","compact":"69f98ae94f11704ec8f2095a1cf20c0d304943733aa97ac34374f200bd7daf94","nasal":"3c28456a34236ca8aadb0b3ab631d2ac0eb072c55a5f6a7a0ce45d1f423f53a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":12,"english":"Hearing Vaidehi's speech pathetic and uttered with tears, the highly energetic Hanumān, son to the Wind-god, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d1888c682306f95ea8ccf10eb94f940f9fdb8cc7f7cb98f59edabfa83681866e","compact":"4eb2649d6e666bca607ebc748908a707a76de4ae351c8eb09c132fc9ffbb2c3f","nasal":"4eb2649d6e666bca607ebc748908a707a76de4ae351c8eb09c132fc9ffbb2c3f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":13,"english":"My revered one, I swear to you by truth itself that Rāma neglect every business because of grief for you. And Rāma being over-whelmed with woe, Laksmana burn in grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee55052eb0fe2b5b569d451f13d761b6d0a2070af37b13c95f5bc39bbfa03f26","compact":"ea6e0935eaccc13d1e18244fd06ece1c36212a6a8cb3036bb00e8b7b47a09e18","nasal":"ea6e0935eaccc13d1e18244fd06ece1c36212a6a8cb3036bb00e8b7b47a09e18"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":14,"english":"Now that I have succeeded in seeing you after no end of ado, this is no time for lamentation. O fair one, this very moment you shall witness the end of your woe.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c35f6214709b7820dafb0cd025e38da99cebeb785a6ae70cbca3c628dddfbe2e","compact":"ee5f23ebecf042658a63d7b22cbac5dba1ee314936127320c1795e92ad3d5374","nasal":"76fd1f0af71614a142a4de14c8ddae6767179ff817a71ee4ef1f399e8d965f2f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":15,"english":"Those blameless princes-foremost of men, gathering courage from my sight of you shall reduce Lankā to ashes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f0a13def207e2da15c2de00d4f64feb926384139bddeae3970d5a1ea94d094f","compact":"a61dc1cbdb1012fe3043f20e2dc250b4870f92a3c72e01e7d74226244695d3da","nasal":"4bad0da865c92190fd1f23789d455b1a6bea50c0fc43e998f79b96df6db22eb1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":16,"english":"O you of expansive eyes, slaying in battle Rāvana along with his friends, Raghu's, sons shall take you back to their own palace.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.478,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6f1d6b891fb41d89438400c0b0d0040fcdcededd1bbbb5479282748b10bfbc6e","compact":"57111a3d9237eebdfeee7d3bcea7d17c81acdb0344307aa9f5627b46853ec7e3","nasal":"821945b30cea84c348f0c0195c50480a1fb39b02c516cb2170138bf64c210289"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":17,"english":"Now, O faultless lady, you ought to give me such a sign as Rāma shall certainly recognise, and as shall more please him by far.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"98f5cd68be159470761a4694f50988b3a0af4f59da7ff4a2f0fed130a9749325","compact":"e7f67e8d7385dcab50eaab279f662d944cab2d59a729ba83249f07eb40098014","nasal":"1731b228349c4a93c4a1edd3517eded30aa6845569b3783de4dcd79cc29b8edb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":18,"english":"“Ah!” (answered Sītā), \"I have already furnished you with an excellent sign. This ornament, . Hanuman, when carefully examined by Rāma, O hero, shall render your words credible.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.771,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3169b3517794762e70c67587fc48e0502513d4a911ede66913b513208d4f1cd8","compact":"6da48338c6b4c5fdbdaae0492b50c3ac89d993aa83b399d8d74955ad8d613591","nasal":"6da48338c6b4c5fdbdaae0492b50c3ac89d993aa83b399d8d74955ad8d613591"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":19,"english":"Thereupon, taking that best of gems, that graceful foremost of monkeys, bowing down the head to that exalted one, prepared to depart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0dd586a6eba08ae2c304a03ec252bb362c5871cdd78238497545b09e0bd78434","compact":"0abcbfd35407ed6b9d67a1e3adf6073fbb19594b127eddc2d60d9159a18c1b1a","nasal":"0abcbfd35407ed6b9d67a1e3adf6073fbb19594b127eddc2d60d9159a18c1b1a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":20,"english":"Seeing that monkey-leader intent upon leaping up, and surcharged with energy, with his person enlarged, Janaka's daughter, with a tearful countenance, spake in woe-begone guise, her accents choked with the vapour of grief,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c024d76f842e9597cd89792d5ecabdc11187eb9342f2ee7191d8e5df6b1b570","compact":"543d45910af7222c1b4ee0d98e038691964cfc2d9233fa2f66e4c277bdeb287a","nasal":"543d45910af7222c1b4ee0d98e038691964cfc2d9233fa2f66e4c277bdeb287a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":21,"english":"O Hanumān, communicate tidings of my good health to those lion-like brothers, Rāma and Laksmana, to' Sugriva along with his counsellors, and to all (the monkeys).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9715ff4dfc9e9d29d52def5dd484b6317fea78ab14915e44f52097a0478d3497","compact":"4c4553b27c8d1faa02f48e244e53517922f89c315163d9491f995a33d3474f34","nasal":"4c4553b27c8d1faa02f48e244e53517922f89c315163d9491f995a33d3474f34"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":22,"english":"And it behove you so to compass things that the mighty-armed Rāghava may rescue me from this sea of sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.689,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d35964de06289e75bef39cf4f8935afc294a6de4f5b2eef97f2dd7f1265e52b","compact":"27dfc1a48f11dcff22ddf5c5f96df2cc46af05a18900544e43b685e45c944d1b","nasal":"63af5b74469d721288caacb4f90f1c4f3678cce7934f051d1eb23d6de3574331"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":23,"english":"Do you, going to Rāma, make known to him the fierce current of my grief, as well as the railing of these Rākşasas. Good fortune be your portion, you exceedingly heroic monkey!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb18d1f6faad09a899a23daddb8f85de7c8ddc74b440062f84171e2991f10fcc","compact":"3e819dddf2c67bdcd05fc93c8638f883f85f3259885d2de6aef5c5512a5ca361","nasal":"3e819dddf2c67bdcd05fc93c8638f883f85f3259885d2de6aef5c5512a5ca361"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-38-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":38,"verse":24,"english":"Thus furnished with the intentions of the princess, the monkey, having gained his object, and, growing exceedingly exhilarated in his heart, reviewed the small work that yet remained for him, became bent upon proceeding to the north.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.685,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-40-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5038024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2985f9907c5dece4ba5265cc2dfa0e92d740e99593b21aebfe3e79d7e25ceacd","compact":"0cd938810be053e5f42269cf3dc6cd7c1497e6b7cbdceb8565be41669f9a2c35","nasal":"0cd938810be053e5f42269cf3dc6cd7c1497e6b7cbdceb8565be41669f9a2c35"}}]
